sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Browser as User Browser
    participant GW as Platform Gateway<br/>HTTPRoute NB_PREFIX<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant KRP as kube-rbac-proxy sidecar<br/>controller-defined port<br/>TLS service CA
    participant JS as Jupyter Server<br/>8888/TCP HTTP
    participant NGX as nginx<br/>8888/TCP HTTP
    participant CS as code-server<br/>8787/TCP HTTP
    participant HT as httpd CGI<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant Culler as Notebook-controller culler
    participant DSP as DSP API server<br/>8888 or 443/TCP HTTPS
    participant S3 as Object storage<br/>endpoint-defined
    participant RT as Pipeline pod<br/>runtime-* image

    Note over Browser,JS: Flow 1 - User opens a JupyterLab workbench
    Browser->>GW: GET NB_PREFIX/lab<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+, OAuth/OIDC session
    GW->>KRP: Forward<br/>HTTPS service CA, Bearer token
    KRP->>KRP: SubjectAccessReview on Notebook
    KRP->>JS: Proxy to 8888/TCP<br/>HTTP pod-local, no auth
    JS->>JS: Kernels/terminals via ZMQ localhost<br/>Kernel HMAC key
    JS-->>KRP: JupyterLab UI / WebSocket
    KRP-->>GW: Response
    GW-->>Browser: Response

    Note over KRP,Culler: Flow 2 - code-server request path
    KRP->>NGX: 8888/TCP HTTP, no auth
    NGX->>CS: NB_PREFIX/codeserver/ to 8787/TCP<br/>HTTP/WebSocket, --auth none
    CS-->>NGX: IDE UI
    Culler->>NGX: GET NB_PREFIX/api/kernels/<br/>8888/TCP HTTP
    NGX->>HT: Proxy to 8080/TCP
    HT->>CS: access.cgi GET /healthz<br/>8787/TCP HTTP
    CS-->>HT: health / last activity
    HT-->>Culler: Jupyter-style kernel activity JSON

    Note over JS,RT: Flow 3 - Elyra pipeline submission and execution
    JS->>S3: Upload notebook + deps archive<br/>HTTPS (or HTTP), access key from runtime Secret
    JS->>DSP: Submit pipeline via KFP SDK<br/>HTTPS TLS, Bearer pod SA token
    DSP->>RT: Argo launches node pod<br/>runtime-* image, pod SA
    RT->>S3: bootstrapper.py download inputs<br/>TLS only if https://, static keys / IRSA
    RT->>S3: Upload outputs
